@startuml platform-channel-flow
' A platform channel message (Discord interaction or WhatsApp event) through the User Gateway and back out through the platform API.
' Source of truth: docs/src/gateways/user/platform-adapters.md
!include _style.puml

actor "Person on\nDiscord or WhatsApp" as user
participant "Platform\n(Discord, Meta)" as plat #FFE4B5
participant "User Gateway\n:8080" as gw #90EE90
participant "Agent Service\n/v1/message" as agent
participant "Platform API\n(gateway-level base URL)" as api #FFE4B5

user -> plat : slash command, or a message
plat -> gw : POST /channels/{ns}/{path}\nsigned by the platform

group #F5F5F5 1. Size check, routing gate, verify
  alt body over maxMessageBodyBytes
    gw --> plat : **413**
  else path not Ready, or signature invalid
    gw --> plat : **401**
  end
end
note over gw
  Discord: Ed25519 over timestamp
  and body, timestamp within 300s.
  WhatsApp: HMAC-SHA256 over the
  body with the app secret.
  A Discord PING and a WhatsApp
  verification GET are answered
  here and go no further.
end note

group #F5F5F5 2. Scope and filter
  alt Discord: outside guildId or allowedChannelIds
    gw --> plat : ephemeral refusal, no envelope
  else WhatsApp: statuses, or another phone number
    gw --> plat : **200**, dropped
  end
end

gw --> plat : **acknowledge**\nDiscord: deferred response (type 5)\nWhatsApp: 200, empty body
note over plat, gw #FFF8DC
  The platform is now gone.
  Everything below runs in the
  async pipeline, with **no**
  kaalm-async record: nobody
  will poll for it.
end note

group #F5F5F5 3. Normalize, wake if needed, deliver
  gw -> gw : one envelope per message
  gw -> agent : POST /v1/message (mTLS)\n4 attempts: 1s, 5s, 25s
  agent --> gw : reply envelope, or an error payload
end

group #F5F5F5 4. SendReply through the platform API
  gw -> api : Discord: follow-up webhook\nWhatsApp: POST /{phoneNumberId}/messages
  alt 2xx
    api --> gw : delivered
    api -> user : the reply shows up in the chat
  else terminal (400, 401, 403, 404, 405, 410, 415)
    api --> gw : refused
    gw -> gw : CallbackRejected on channel health,\nWarning event, payload dropped
  else retried (connect, timeout, 408, 429, 5xx)
    api --> gw : retry on the callback schedule
  end
end
@enduml
